 </div>
 </div>

 <p class="text-center text-sm text-slate-600 mt-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">For OEM buyers: one Qi2-certified SKU now serves both iOS and Android premium users. No need for separate magnetic and non-magnetic inventory.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- N52H Magnet Technology -->
<section id="n52h-magnet-technology" class="sec bg-slate-50 relative" data-section="content">
 <div class="container-wide">
 <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic tracking-tighter mb-4 text-center">N52H Magnet Technology: <span class="text-brandOrange">Why Grade Matters</span></h2>
 <p class="text-center text-slate-500 text-sm max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">All WOWOHCOOL Qi2 power banks use N52H neodymium magnets — not the cheaper N35 or N48 found in budget products. Here's why the H grade matters for wireless charging reliability.</p>

 <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
 <div class="card p-6 shadow-sm">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3 text-sm">N52 (Standard)</h3>
 <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
 <li>&bull; BH(max): 52 MGOe</li>
 <li>&bull; Max working temp: <strong class="text-red-500">60°C</strong></li>
 <li>&bull; Risk: Wireless charging heats to 40-55°C — near thermal limit</li>
 <li>&bull; Over time: Gradual demagnetization = weaker snap</li>
 </ul>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-brandOrange/30 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-brandOrange/20">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandOrange uppercase mb-3 text-sm">N52H (WOWOHCOOL Standard)</h3>
 <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
 <li>&bull; BH(max): 52 MGOe (same strength)</li>
 <li>&bull; Max working temp: <strong class="text-green-600">120°C</strong></li>
 <li>&bull; 2x thermal headroom above charging temps</li>
 <li>&bull; Zero demagnetization risk over product lifetime</li>
 </ul>
 </div>
 </div>
 <p class="text-center text-xs text-slate-400 mt-6">N52H costs 15-20% more than N52 but eliminates the #1 cause of magnetic power bank warranty returns: weakened alignment after 6-12 months of use.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section id="faq" class="sec bg-slate-50" data-section="faq">
 <div class="container-narrow">
 {{ sectionHeader('FAQ', 'Wireless / Magnetic <span class="text-brandOrange">FAQ</span>', '', {max: ''}) }}
 <div class="reveal">
 {% call faqItem("What is Qi2 vs Qi?", true) %}Qi2 is the second generation of the Qi wireless charging standard, adding magnetic alignment (MPP - Magnetic Power Profile) and 15W universal fast charging. It's based on Apple's MagSafe technology and works with iPhone 12-16 series natively.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("What is the MOQ for Qi2 wireless power banks?", true) %}MOQ starts at 500 units for standard ODM models with custom logo. ODM new-design development: 1,000-2,000 units. OEM with new tooling: 3,000+ units. Sample turnaround 3-7 days for pre-production samples.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("Are these MagSafe compatible?", true) %}Yes. Qi2 is built on Apple's MagSafe standard. Our power banks use N52H neodymium magnets for the same alignment strength as Apple's MagSafe accessories.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("Can it charge through a phone case?") %}Yes, through cases up to 4mm thick. For magnetic alignment, the case must be MagSafe-compatible (most premium cases support this). Pure plastic cases without metal interference work universally.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("What is the difference between Qi2 and MagSafe?") %}Qi2 is the open standard version of MagSafe, managed by WPC (Wireless Power Consortium). MagSafe is Apple's proprietary implementation. Both use the same magnetic ring and 15W speed, but Qi2 works cross-platform — iPhone 12-16 plus Android phones like Samsung Galaxy S25 and Google Pixel 10. For OEM buyers, Qi2 certification means your product is automatically MagSafe-compatible without needing Apple MFi licensing.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("Which Android phones support Qi2 magnetic charging?") %}As of mid-2026, Samsung Galaxy S25 series and Google Pixel 10 series support native Qi2 magnetic alignment. More Android flagships are expected in 2026 H2. This means Qi2 magnetic power banks now address both iPhone AND Android premium users — effectively doubling the total addressable market for your brand.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("What is N52H magnet and why does it matter?") %}N52H is a neodymium magnet grade with 52 MGOe energy and a working temperature up to 120°C (vs 60°C for standard N52). Since wireless charging generates 40-55°C heat, N52H prevents demagnetization during prolonged charging — maintaining snap alignment strength over the product's full lifetime. Budget competitors using N52 or N48 magnets often develop weak alignment within 6-12 months.{% endcall %}
 {% call faqItem("What is Qi2.2 and 25W wireless charging?") %}Qi2.2 is the latest WPC standard (released 2025) enabling 25W magnetic wireless charging — a 67% speed increase over Qi2's 15W. First Qi2.2 products launched in 2026 from Belkin, EcoFlow, and Baseus. It's backward-compatible with existing Qi2 15W devices. WOWOHCOOL offers Qi2.2 25W OEM models for brands wanting next-gen speed positioning.{% endcall %}
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

